// field.c -- the interactive field in C + SDL2 (the Belthasar host): the player walks a scene, NPC scripts run on
// the C VM, dialogue, doors, foreground priority, camera and collision. Reads ct_assets.dat only.
//
//   Arrow keys : walk    X (hold) : run (pad B, the Dash row, $00F8 bit 1)    Space / Z / Enter : talk / advance (A)
//   C : menu (the SNES X button; B = X key / Backspace closes it)    Esc : quit
// Usage: Belthasar[.exe] --assets ct_assets.dat [--scene N] [--loadflags <f>]
//        [--selftest [out.raw]] [--talk <obj>] [--gotoexit]      (the debug modes: docs/DEBUG_SURFACE.md)
//   --boot            the game's cold entry (disasm/notes/boot_loader.md): C0/0057's SRAM scan, then scene 0's
//                     boot script (title, then the load screen or a new game). Enter = START. The 8 KB battery
//                     is ct_sram.srm (CT_SRAM overrides it; CT_SRAM_FRESH=1 boots an erased cart).
//   --loadcheck <srm> run FF/FAA3 over an SRAM image and print each slot's unpacked fields.
//   --sramcheck <srm> run the ROM's FF/FBE7 checksum over an SRAM image, per slot.
